4. Restrictions
   You may not reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble xDev, except
   where such restriction is prohibited by applicable law.

5. Third-party components
   xDev includes third-party components (LLVM, LLD, libc++, mingw-w64,
   SDL3, GLFW and others) that remain under their own licenses, listed in
   the lib/licenses/ folder. Nothing in this license limits your rights
   under those licenses.

   NOTE! The xDev curl library (lib/xdev/libxcurl.a) contains GNU libiconv
   (LGPL-2.1 or later), libidn2 and libunistring (LGPL-3.0 or later, or
   GPL-2.0 or later). These components are statically linked into every
   program that uses the curl functions of xDev. Point 2 does not apply to
   them. If you distribute such a program, you must comply with the terms
   of those licenses, in particular include their license texts and allow
   the recipients to relink your program with modified versions of these
   libraries, for example by providing the object files of your program.
   Programs that do not use the curl functions do not contain these
   components and are covered by point 2 without restriction.

